Good afternoon,


I appreciate your offer and I am willing to negotiate with you.

The major issue that Thorwin Properties faces is not following protocol
stated by the RTB. I have not received Form 8 ( Notice to Tenant =E2=80=93
Reduction/Withdrawal of Service) related to the withdrawal of the laundry
service and storage unit. I had inquired about the plans on July 7, 2023 to
Darren Wilcox and Thorwin Properties has had the opportunity to file the
required forms since and before then but I did not receive a response.
Non-compliance by Thorwin Properties to Manitoba legislation will lead to
financial loss due to undone due diligence and failure to follow protocol.

I have stated several times that I do not want the renovations proposed as
the services are included in my original Lease Agreement with Winpark
Dorchester and these services are grandfathered into my current lease with
Thorwin Properties as stated by Property Manager Celena Funk on Friday, May
5, 2023. She also stated, "The Mobile Resident Manager was unaware that
your storage locker had been grandfathered in prior to Thorwin Properties
purchase of the building. Should at any time we decide to remove the
storage units we will apply through the Residential Tenancy Branch for a
withdrawal of service."

The RTB has provided me with alternative information from what you have
presented to me - Form 9 must be completed by the landlord. Can you tell me
the name of the individual you have consulted with at the RTB in regards to
protocol?


My counter proposals are as follows:

1. Thorwin Properties follows protocol and applies with Form 9 to the RTB
and I receive Form 8. There is a reasonable expectation that renovation
delivery will be 3 months from application date. Following receipt of Form
8 we would then negotiate based on the changes of services approved by the
RTB.

OR

2. If I agree to the proposal of renovations stated in your email on
Friday, Jan 5, 2024 that would begin on January 22 and end on February 2,
2024 then the following updated agreement will be honoured:

*"The landlord would like to propose a conditional rent discount for month
by month in the amount of $500.00 to compensate for affecting the tenant's
quality of living and mental health. The proposed tenancy agreement and
rent discount will be indefinite and will be applied January 1, 2024 and
can only be terminated through mutual agreement between tenant and
landlord. Failure to pay rent on time for three instances will result in
the termination of the conditional rent agreement."*

In addition to the agreement to rent discount, the following will be
provided to the tenant:

   1. An additional discount for January rent in the amount of $375.00 to
   compensate for affecting your quality of living on Day 1-8,
   2. 24/7 access to 3-585 Corydon Ave from January 22, 2024 - February 2,
   2024,
   3. Purchase and installation of storage unit in 10-585 Corydon Ave based
   on the tenants discretion and fulfilled by Thorwin Properties of no more
   than $500 value after tax.

You mentioned that you believe that rent increase is the issue and I have
attached a chart illustrating the issue.

I look forward to hearing back from you.

All the best,
Evan Rosner

